{
  "title": "No Fold Certificate of Darkness Below 21 Walls in Orthogonal Lattice Rooms",
  "version": "0.1",
  "date": "2026-11-23",
  "scope": "Computer-assisted: no strictly simple orthogonal lattice room with W <= 20 has a rational interior pair certified dark by Par, Cut, or Rig certificates over any pillowcase base. Includes a second proof of the core case by fold enumeration, the fold-converse lemma, and a separate result that an R22-type parity fold needs r >= 9. Shows only that this certificate mechanism produces no dark pair; does not show that every pair is lit.",
